      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "Research suggests that a balanced approach that incorporates elements of both robust border enforcement and pathways to citizenship is likely to provide the most sustainable solution. This is because addressing the root causes of migration while also providing a clear and efficient process for newcomers to integrate into society can help to alleviate economic and social pressures. A path that focuses too heavily on enforcement alone may lead to reduced influx of migrants, but may also deter those who are fleeing persecution or seeking better opportunities.",
